{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtRVt8tkWfMxTcnBbdRT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A memory write should no longer evict the static instructions. I split the system prompt into two cached blocks in `bot.py` and wrote up the details in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't confirmed this against the live API because there's no key here.\n\n**What changed:** `build_system()` used to put the instructions and the per-athlete context in one block with one cache marker. Any change to the facts changed the prefix hash and evicted everything. It now returns two blocks, each with its own `cache_control`:\n1. The static `INSTRUCTIONS`, identical for every athlete and every day.\n2. The volatile tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language).\n\nA `save_fact` now only invalidates the tail. I left the tools, model, tool loop and usage logging untouched.\n\n**Checked offline:** I called `build_system()` directly. Block 1 stays byte-identical across athletes, dates and fact changes, and block 2 changes when a fact is added.\n\n**Still to check:** Sonnet-class models only cache prefixes of roughly 1024 tokens or more. Tools plus instructions is probably just above that, but I couldn't confirm it. If it's below, the marker on block 1 is silently ignored and memory writes will evict the static part again. The check is in `ANSWER.md`: after a `save_fact`, `cache_read_input_tokens` should cover the tools and instructions, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` should be roughly the tail, tens of tokens for one athlete.\n\nTool-group changes from the keyword filter still evict both blocks, since tools sit above the system prompt. That's existing behaviour and I left it alone.\n\n`ANSWER.md` also records which parts of the colleague's note applied. The two-marker split and the byte-stability rule did. The top-N selection, tail reordering and token figures didn't apply to this code.\n\nThe change is uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2796,"cache_read_input_tokens":35627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2796},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7668131f-0105-4e1e-a20d-d69568a8e9ed","uuid":"ffb6461e-81bf-4ec1-b724-46ff4730a4a6","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:01:31.083Z","request_id":"req_011CgtRVsyUVFnZbQT8zDsdT"}
